ctors"},{"text":"3D vectors"},{"text":"Dot product"},{"text":"Cross product"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Direction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Matrices"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transformation matrices"},{"text":"Rotation"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Scaling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Coordinate systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"World space"},{"text":"Local space"},{"text":"Camera space"},{"text":"Screen space"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rotations"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Euler angles"},{"text":"Rotation matrices"},{"text":"Quaternions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Raycasting"},{"text":"Projection"},{"text":"Interpolation"},{"text":"Transformations"},{"text":"Coordinate conversion"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A developer who understands these concepts can debug spatial behaviour rather than treating the game engine as a black box."}]},{"heading":"Choose a game engine","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Unity route"},{"type":"p","text":"For many beginners, Unity + C# provides a practical entry point."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity Editor"},{"text":"Scenes"},{"text":"GameObjects"},{"text":"Components"},{"text":"Prefabs"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Cameras"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"UI"},{"text":"C# scripting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Unity architecture"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Scene","GameObjects","Components","Scripts","Physics / Rendering / Input"]},{"type":"h","text":"Unreal Engine route"},{"type":"p","text":"For students targeting high-end graphics and larger game/visualisation environments:"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unreal Editor"},{"text":"Actors"},{"text":"Components"},{"text":"Blueprints"},{"text":"C++"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Level design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended approach"},{"type":"p","text":"Don't try to master Unity and Unreal simultaneously."},{"type":"p","text":"Choose:"},{"type":"h","text":"Unity first → Unreal later if career direction requires it"}]},{"heading":"3D development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D assets"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Textures"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Cameras"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"Particle systems"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Colliders"},{"text":"Rigid bodies"},{"text":"Audio"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D modelling"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Blender"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic modelling"},{"text":"UV mapping"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Texturing"},{"text":"Rigging"},{"text":"Animation"},{"text":"Exporting 3D assets"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The developer does not need to become a professional 3D artist, but understanding the asset pipeline is valuable."}]},{"heading":"Game development fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Even if the target is enterprise AR/VR, game-development concepts are extremely useful."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game loops"},{"text":"Input systems"},{"text":"State machines"},{"text":"Collision detection"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Animation systems"},{"text":"Scene management"},{"text":"UI"},{"text":"Audio"},{"text":"Save systems"},{"text":"Object pooling"},{"text":"Performance optimisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Architecture"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Input","Game Logic","Physics","Animation","Rendering"]}]},{"heading":"AR development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the fundamentals of augmented reality."},{"type":"h","text":"Concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Plane detection"},{"text":"Image tracking"},{"text":"Object tracking"},{"text":"Anchors"},{"text":"Raycasting"},{"text":"Spatial mapping"},{"text":"Occlusion"},{"text":"World tracking"},{"text":"Camera tracking"},{"text":"Lighting estimation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mobile AR"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore platform-specific frameworks such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ARCore"},{"text":"ARKit"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use the current supported engine/plugin integrations rather than relying on outdated packages."}]},{"heading":"VR development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Head tracking"},{"text":"6DoF"},{"text":"Controllers"},{"text":"Hand tracking"},{"text":"Teleportation"},{"text":"Room-scale interaction"},{"text":"Spatial audio"},{"text":"Haptics"},{"text":"Grab/interact systems"},{"text":"Locomotion"},{"text":"Comfort design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important VR design principles"},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid unnecessary:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion sickness"},{"text":"Excessive camera movement"},{"text":"Poor frame rates"},{"text":"Uncomfortable locomotion"},{"text":"Overly complex interactions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Comfort is a technical requirement, not merely a UX preference."}]},{"heading":"XR standards and interaction","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn modern XR concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OpenXR"},{"text":"XR input"},{"text":"Hand tracking"},{"text":"Eye tracking"},{"text":"Spatial anchors"},{"text":"Passthrough"},{"text":"Mixed reality"},{"text":"Spatial mapping"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is to understand cross-device XR development rather than building everything around one headset."}]},{"heading":"Computer vision","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AR/VR increasingly overlaps with computer vision."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the basics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Image processing"},{"text":"Feature detection"},{"text":"Object detection"},{"text":"Image classification"},{"text":"Camera calibration"},{"text":"Pose estimation"},{"text":"Depth estimation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OpenCV"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Computer vision libraries"},{"text":"ML frameworks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You don't need to become a computer-vision researcher, but these skills can be valuable for advanced AR applications."}]},{"heading":"AI + XR","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI creates another major career direction."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how AI can support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gesture recognition"},{"text":"Hand tracking"},{"text":"Object recognition"},{"text":"Voice interfaces"},{"text":"AI characters"},{"text":"Spatial understanding"},{"text":"Personalised virtual environments"},{"text":"Generative 3D content"},{"text":"Natural-language interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"flow","items":["User speaks","speech recognition","AI model","decision","virtual character responds"]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a powerful combination:"},{"type":"flow","items":["XR","AI","Computer Vision"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Spatial computing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Go beyond traditional VR games."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spatial interfaces"},{"text":"3D UI"},{"text":"Persistent spatial anchors"},{"text":"Environment understanding"},{"text":"Digital twins"},{"text":"Real-world/virtual-world interaction"},{"text":"Spatial audio"},{"text":"Multimodal interaction"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial training"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"Engineering"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Retail"},{"text":"Remote assistance"}]}]},{"heading":"Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build 4–6 substantial projects."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — AR product visualiser"},{"type":"p","tex